<h1>Brittany B. Kimble</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 6b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Kimble has made CPS budget discipline the center of her campaign, opposing high-interest short-term borrowing to plug shortfalls. She also emphasizes improving literacy and math proficiency and ensuring students with IEPs and 504 plans receive the special education services they are entitled to, and argues her legal background handling contracts and personnel disputes prepared her to oversee the district.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Attorney who has run her own law practice since 2010, handling criminal defense, domestic relations, and real estate cases; appointed chair of the Illinois Employment Security Board of Review by Gov. Pritzker in 2023. She is a CPS parent.</p>
